---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Easiest Baby Nasal Aspirator to Clean at 3AM | QuietBabyGear";
const description = "A QuietBabyGear timed cleaning test comparing baby nasal aspirators under low-light, sleep-deprived parent conditions.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">MCT test draft</p>
    <h1>Easiest Baby Nasal Aspirator to Clean at 3AM</h1>
    <p class="lead">This page will compare the first five aspirators using QuietBabyGear's Midnight Cleaning Time test. Results will be published after timed cleaning trials and original test media are complete.</p>

    <h2>Short conclusion</h2>
    <p>Pending first-party testing. The final conclusion will identify the easiest aspirator to clean at night, the product with the highest cleanup friction, and who should avoid each model.</p>

    <h2>Data table</h2>
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Product</th>
          <th>MCT</th>
          <th>Parts to clean</th>
          <th>One-hand friction</th>
          <th>Leakage notes</th>
          <th>Status</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Frida NoseFrida</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Awaiting test</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Grownsy Electric</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Awaiting test</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Nosiboo Pro</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Awaiting test</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Braun Electric</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Planned</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Momcozy BreezyClear</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Pending</td><td>Planned</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>How we will test</h2>
    <p>Each aspirator will be used in the same low-light setup. We will start a stopwatch after use, disassemble the parts that require cleaning, rinse them according to the product instructions, set them to dry, and stop the timer when the product is reasonably reset for the next use.</p>

    <h2>Original test media needed</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Stopwatch start and finish photos.</li>
      <li>Parts layout after disassembly.</li>
      <li>Cleaning process photos under warm low light.</li>
      <li>Water residue or hard-to-dry areas.</li>
      <li>One-handed handling notes.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <h3>Is this medical advice?</h3>
    <p>No. This test only compares product handling, cleaning friction, and real-world usability.</p>
    <h3>Why focus on cleaning time?</h3>
    <p>Because a product that feels manageable during the day can feel very different when a parent is exhausted and trying not to wake the room.</p>
    <h3>Will affiliate links affect the ranking?</h3>
    <p>No. Affiliate links may be added after testing, but the timing data and notes stay independent.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

